WEBVTT

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:04.090
We have a conical tank is nine meters deep with a
radius of three meters at the top.

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:08.690
Water enters at four meters squared per minute.
How fast is the depth when the water

00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:13.350
is six meters deep? Again, let's do our same
process of finding our knowns and

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:17.990
unknowns and then finding our equation and
then subbing those in to find our

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:21.550
unknown, subbing our knowns in to find our
unknown. So from the beginning here, in

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:24.970
our first sentence, we're told it's a conical
tank. That's our first piece of

00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:27.930
information. So we know what
shape this tank is in.

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:32.790
We know that the height of this tank is 9
meters deep. So we got one of the

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:33.190
variables.

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:37.510
And we are told that the
radius is 3 meters.

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:44.320
So now we know the shape, the height, and the
radius. And we're told when filling up

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:49.220
this tank, water enters at 4 meters squared per
minute. So now we know the rate of

00:00:49.070 --> 00:00:50.080
our volume.

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:56.500
Thirdly, we're told how fast the depth when the
water is six meters deep. So this is

00:00:56.350 --> 00:01:00.660
what we have to find out. We have to find how
fast the depth is. So what's the rate

00:01:00.510 --> 00:01:04.840
of the depth? And we have to find it when the
water is six meters deep. So this

00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:09.180
whole thing is our question, not just that first
part. And because we're told it's

00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:12.400
going to be at six meters, that's also another
piece of given information that can

00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:17.140
help us find it because we know we have to
substitute six in when we're getting that

00:01:16.990 --> 00:01:18.160
rate of the depth.

00:01:19.030 --> 00:01:24.580
So the next piece in our formula, in our
systematic formula for solving, would

00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:28.600
be getting an equation that models it. Well,
we know we're having, we have two

00:01:28.450 --> 00:01:32.920
variables. We know we have an r variable. We know
we have an h variable. And we know

00:01:32.770 --> 00:01:38.300
it's the velocity, volume of the cone. So even
without those two variables, we

00:01:38.150 --> 00:01:43.660
know that we're going to have to do V equals
1 over 3 pi r squared h because

00:01:43.510 --> 00:01:47.900
we're dealing with volume and we're dealing
with these variables and the rates.

00:01:47.870 --> 00:01:49.060
Everything has to do with this equation.

00:01:49.830 --> 00:01:54.340
So our next step, just like our last two
questions, would be to take the derivative

00:01:54.190 --> 00:01:58.960
of this with respect to time. But before I do
that, I want to mention something

00:01:58.810 --> 00:02:03.740
because there's actually two ways of solving
this question. And the second way,

00:02:03.770 --> 00:02:07.920
which I'm going to do after I show you the
regular way we've been doing it, is how a

00:02:07.770 --> 00:02:12.520
lot of classes and textbooks usually teach how
to solve this related rates problem.

00:02:12.370 --> 00:02:16.540
but I think it makes much more sense to follow
through what we've been doing for the

00:02:16.390 --> 00:02:19.880
last two questions first and then
teaching you that second approach

00:02:21.410 --> 00:02:26.240
To continue on this formula we would take the
derivative with respect to time so here

00:02:26.090 --> 00:02:31.390
that would be dv over dt
equals 1 over 3 pi and

00:02:34.010 --> 00:02:37.740
then you're gonna have a bracket here and
then we're gonna have d r squared

00:02:38.490 --> 00:02:44.090
over dt times h plus r squared

00:02:43.940 --> 00:02:48.650
dh over dt now if you're confused on what we did
here because it looks a little bit

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:53.670
than the last two because we have both these
variables that are gonna be derived

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:58.870
with dt we're using our product rule and
obviously just like our first

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:02.830
example we have a factor here that doesn't have
any variables related to it so you

00:03:02.680 --> 00:03:06.650
don't have to do any we don't have to derive
these by dt because they're just a

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:11.300
factor. Now expanding one more step
we would get 1 over 3 pi

00:03:11.850 --> 00:03:17.460
2r dr 2rh dr over

00:03:17.310 --> 00:03:21.960
dt plus r squared dh over dt.

00:03:22.710 --> 00:03:27.780
This is all equal to dv over dt. So now
we have our first equation

00:03:27.630 --> 00:03:32.560
when without the rates and our second
equation with the rates.

00:03:32.930 --> 00:03:38.380
So let's see what from these two equations can
we fill out based on the givens that

00:03:38.230 --> 00:03:41.520
we have in the question. Well, starting with
the second equation, we're told that

00:03:41.370 --> 00:03:45.680
waters enter at four meters squared per
minute. So this is a given, so we can

00:03:45.530 --> 00:03:46.520
underline it with black.

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:52.980
And we also know that we need to find how fast
the depth is when the water is at six

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:58.460
meters. So because this is our question, we're
going to plug in the six, not the

00:03:58.310 --> 00:04:01.580
nine, because the nine is at the full tank but we
don't care what's at the full tank

00:04:01.430 --> 00:04:07.000
we only care when the water is six meters deep
so that means we have this h but

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:12.390
we do not have these r's because again we need
to find out what the r is when the

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:15.350
water is six meters deep not what we've been
given in the question which is three

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:19.750
meters deep so the r's we can have them as red
because these are what we need to

00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:24.970
these are part of the two part of the
steps we would take to

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:30.400
find our final answer and then for
our dr over t we're also

00:04:30.250 --> 00:04:35.700
not given the rate of r so we're going to
have to find this as well before we

00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:40.520
find what the question is asking us which is how
fast the depth is which is our dh

00:04:40.370 --> 00:04:45.510
over dt so we know that we need to

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:51.000
find dh over dt by first finding what

00:04:50.850 --> 00:04:56.260
our r and dr over dt is okay so how can we

00:04:56.110 --> 00:05:01.560
find what our r and dr over dt is well
first we can start by just

00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:07.000
trying to find our r and again if
whenever we get stuck on

00:05:06.850 --> 00:05:11.260
what where to go next just like our last
example it's easiest if we just model

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:14.920
what's happening with a diagram it's a little
bit harder to draw these three

00:05:14.770 --> 00:05:19.160
diagrams and i'm going to try my best i'm going
to draw a circle and a cone here and

00:05:19.010 --> 00:05:23.540
we're going to imagine the height is at 6. So
this is like majority. We'll say the h

00:05:23.390 --> 00:05:24.840
here is 6 meters, okay?

00:05:25.650 --> 00:05:31.300
Because we know the full height is 9
meters and the radius

00:05:31.150 --> 00:05:36.060
is 3 meters, then we know that

00:05:35.910 --> 00:05:41.400
here the radius is one -third of the height.
So you could say here that the

00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:46.890
radius equals one -third of h, okay?
And because this cone

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:51.950
is straight and not jagged, we know that this
relationship of r equals 1 over

00:05:51.800 --> 00:05:54.610
3h is going to be consistent
throughout the full cone.

00:05:55.270 --> 00:06:00.140
So what we can do is in this
equation, we can substitute r

00:06:00.310 --> 00:06:04.520
with 1 over 3h. So we can have 1 over 3 pi

00:06:04.560 --> 00:06:06.870
is 2

00:06:08.130 --> 00:06:13.640
times 1 over 3 h or h

00:06:13.490 --> 00:06:18.090
over 3 times h times dr over dt

00:06:18.350 --> 00:06:23.090
plus h over 3 all squared

00:06:22.940 --> 00:06:28.410
dh over dt. So now we have changed

00:06:28.260 --> 00:06:33.450
dr to h and we already know what our h is
because our h is 6. So all that's left is

00:06:33.300 --> 00:06:38.630
for us to find what dr over dt
is. But if you have a

00:06:38.480 --> 00:06:40.030
rate for

00:06:40.270 --> 00:06:45.880
what r

00:06:45.730 --> 00:06:50.320
is going to be when you have h or what h is
when you have r, because, again, this

00:06:50.170 --> 00:06:55.320
cone is straight and it doesn't go out, it's
not jagged, it's just linear, as we

00:06:55.170 --> 00:07:00.300
would call it, That means if the
relationship between r and h is 1 over 3,

00:07:00.430 --> 00:07:05.680
then the relationship between dr and dh
is also going to be 1 over 3.

00:07:05.750 --> 00:07:11.320
So that means dr over dt equals 1
over 3 dh over dt.

00:07:12.070 --> 00:07:17.680
Using this, we can plug the same thing into our
equation down here, and it will become

00:07:17.530 --> 00:07:22.930
1 over 3 pi, 2 times h

00:07:22.780 --> 00:07:27.140
over 3 squared times

00:07:27.440 --> 00:07:32.370
1 over 3, dh over dt,

00:07:34.300 --> 00:07:37.790
plus h squared over 9,

00:07:38.690 --> 00:07:41.200
dh over dt,

00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:48.490
and this all equals dv over dt
but because we know

00:07:48.340 --> 00:07:53.670
our dv over dt from the top and we know our
h we can solve for dh over dt

00:07:53.520 --> 00:07:58.090
by rearranging and solving because i want to
leave some space for the second

00:07:57.940 --> 00:08:03.530
scenario you guys can figure out how to
move this all on your own and

00:08:03.380 --> 00:08:09.010
then I'm pretty sure dh over dt will
equal 1 over pi, and that

00:08:08.860 --> 00:08:12.900
is our final answer. Now that we've done the first
approach, the second scenario is

00:08:12.750 --> 00:08:14.920
actually much easier to see
what's happening.

00:08:16.430 --> 00:08:19.980
All that we're going to do in the second scenario
that's different than the first is

00:08:19.830 --> 00:08:25.440
instead of taking the v equals 1 over 2
pi r squared h's derivative,

00:08:26.710 --> 00:08:32.320
here we're going to first plug in that
relationship we found between r and h into

00:08:32.170 --> 00:08:36.360
this equation, and then we're going to take the
derivative. So the only difference

00:08:36.210 --> 00:08:41.220
is before we're taking the derivative,
we're going to plug in 1 over

00:08:41.070 --> 00:08:46.240
3h squared in place of this r squared. So
now we're going to have v equals

00:08:46.090 --> 00:08:51.600
1 over 3 pi r squared h, and
we're going to remove

00:08:51.450 --> 00:08:56.820
that r, and we're going to put h over 3 in this
bracket, and that's going to give

00:08:56.670 --> 00:09:02.240
us 1 over 27 pi h

00:09:02.090 --> 00:09:05.900
cubed, right? Because this 3 is going to be
squared multiplied by another 3. That's

00:09:05.750 --> 00:09:11.280
3 cubed, which is 27, pi h cubed. And now what
we're going to do is we're going to

00:09:11.130 --> 00:09:16.180
derive with respect to t. So we're going
to take dv over dt equals 1 over

00:09:16.030 --> 00:09:21.260
27 pi 3h squared times

00:09:21.110 --> 00:09:26.300
dh over dt. This 3 is going to reduce
with this 27 to get 9.

00:09:26.190 --> 00:09:31.720
So we're going to be left with 1
over 9 pi h squared dh

00:09:31.570 --> 00:09:35.760
over dt. This is all equal to dv over dt.

00:09:36.950 --> 00:09:41.980
And now all that's left is we plug in
that dv over dt with 4

00:09:41.830 --> 00:09:44.320
meters squared per minute.

00:09:45.540 --> 00:09:50.890
And we plug in the h with 6. So it's
going to become 6 squared

00:09:50.740 --> 00:09:56.000
pi over 9. This is all equal to dh

00:09:55.850 --> 00:10:00.560
over dt. You will get the same
answer of dh over dt

00:10:00.410 --> 00:10:05.840
equals one over pi meters

00:10:05.690 --> 00:10:10.350
per minute. This is why I like doing both scenarios
because in the first scenario, you

00:10:10.200 --> 00:10:14.910
can see just like how we're doing our last
previous examples, how the systematic

00:10:14.760 --> 00:10:20.170
process works. And then upon knowing how it
works, you can figure out the shorter

00:10:20.020 --> 00:10:25.190
version by switching our variables because we
have this linear relationship.

00:10:25.300 --> 00:10:29.870
And what I meant a little early, in case you guys
didn't understand, with the jagged

00:10:29.720 --> 00:10:34.370
edges I was talking about for the cone, we know
that these two relationships hold

00:10:34.220 --> 00:10:39.750
true because we know that our cone is going to
be straight if for example instead

00:10:39.600 --> 00:10:44.550
you had a cone that was like this for the first
part but then it goes like that for

00:10:44.400 --> 00:10:47.370
the second part first of all it wouldn't be
called the cone this is more like a

00:10:47.220 --> 00:10:52.830
funnel shape but we would not have an accurate
representation of what our r and h

00:10:52.680 --> 00:10:58.250
was because here if you let's say we have six
meters you would assume that your r is

00:10:58.100 --> 00:11:00.190
two meters using r 1 to 3 relationship.

00:11:01.060 --> 00:11:06.530
But up here, it would not be the same,
your r versus your h, because

00:11:06.380 --> 00:11:11.230
now your r is much further out, so that
relationship is different. But because we

00:11:11.080 --> 00:11:15.630
have a cone shape and we know it's linear
between the two variables, then we know

00:11:15.480 --> 00:11:20.570
that not only is a relationship for r and h going
to be 1 over 3, but a relationship

00:11:20.420 --> 00:11:26.070
for dr over dt is going to equal 1 over 3 dh over
dt. Thank you, and I'll see you in

00:11:25.920 --> 00:11:26.670
the next episode.
